      "id": 1,
      "text": "Warm Beach was renamed in 1924 after a community founded by real‑estate developer Clarence Dayton Hillman.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warm_Beach%2C_Washington",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hillman sold 12,000 acres in 1906 and operated an excursion steamer that staged a fake city with actors to attract buyers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warm_Beach%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fort Worden, built in the late 1800s as part of Puget Sound’s coastal defense, now stands as a historic site in Warm Beach.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://beckdc.com/historical-places-in-warm-beach/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Warm Beach Church, over a century old, continues to serve as a place of worship and community gathering for residents.",
